OL,3,ASuspected bomb hoax threats force fresh
OL,4,Aevacuations of Italian schools
OL,5,
OL,6,FSchools across Italy have received bomb
OL,7,Fthreats for the second day in a row,
OL,8,Fsparking fresh panic and evacuations.
OL,10,FSome 1,800 schools, from Milan in the
OL,11,Fnorth to Sicily in the south, reported
OL,12,Freceiving a similar threat to one that
OL,13,Fcreated chaos in Italy on Wednesday -
OL,14,Feven though no devices have been found
OL,15,Fanywhere.
OL,17,FThe Italian government has advised
OL,18,Fschools that "in the absence of
OL,19,Fconcrete evidence beyond the simple
OL,20,Freceipt of a mass email indicating a
OL,21,Fdanger, buildings must not not be
OL,22,Fevacuated".
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,316,300,200,140,0,100
